# Stakeholder Power/Interest Matrix – IWMS Project

**Purpose**  
This matrix helps the project team understand how to engage different stakeholders based on their level of **Power** (influence) and **Interest** in the project. It is simple and visual so both technical and non-technical team members can easily understand engagement priorities.

---

### Power/Interest Matrix

|                          | **Low Interest**                                      | **High Interest**                                      |
|--------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
| **High Power**           | **Keep Satisfied**<br><br>• Company Secretary<br>• Head of Procurement | **Manage Closely**<br><br>• Chief Operating Officer (COO)<br>• Chief Financial Officer (CFO)<br>• Head of IT<br>• HR Manager |
| **Low Power**            | **Monitor**<br><br>• Finance / Accounting Team       | **Keep Informed**<br><br>• Property Manager<br>• Construction / Project Architect<br>• Prospective Tenants |

---

### Axis Labels (for clarity)

- **Vertical Axis (Power)**: Influence or decision-making authority on the project  
- **Horizontal Axis (Interest)**: Level of concern or involvement in the project outcomes

---

### Stakeholder Engagement Strategy

| Quadrant          | Stakeholders                                      | Recommended Approach                                      |
|-------------------|---------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| **Manage Closely**    | COO, CFO, Head of IT, HR Manager                 | Frequent meetings, detailed updates, involve in key decisions |
| **Keep Satisfied**    | Company Secretary, Head of Procurement           | Periodic updates, address concerns quickly               |
| **Keep Informed**     | Property Managers, Architects, Prospective Tenants | Regular communication, demos, training sessions          |
| **Monitor**           | Finance / Accounting Team                        | Occasional updates, escalate only when needed            |

---

### Why This Artifact Is Valuable

- Shows you can **analyze and prioritize stakeholders** effectively
- Demonstrates strong **client engagement and consensus-building** skills


